{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Duct tape felt somewhat relevant because it can help with practical repairs alongside the fasteners I recently bought, though I would skip five rolls without a specific project.",
    "Some repair supplies reflected my interest in hands-on hardware tasks, but none felt like a strong immediate choice."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Electrical tape and wire connector kits assume a wiring project; my nuts, bolts, washers, and magnetic hooks point more directly to fastening and mounting.",
    "The stethoscope, inspection camera, and sanding discs require specific tasks that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Bulk trash bags and masks do not address a current need I have expressed, so I would leave them alone."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations treated a broad connection to tools and supplies as enough, when the particular job an item serves matters much more to me.",
    "My purchases of fastener assortments seemed to be taken as interest in large packs generally, but I only want quantities that suit the task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Two recent magnetic-hook purchases make hooks and magnetic mounting a clearer interest than electrical work or specialized inspection.",
    "My closely spaced purchases of washers, nuts, bolts, and hooks suggest a connected fastening or mounting need worth paying attention to.",
    "I rarely interact unless something is relevant now; a potentially useful general supply is not enough to make me choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical hardware interests but stretched them into unrelated tasks instead of staying close to fastening and magnetic mounting."
}"}
